# ShellInABox Configuration Template
# This template generates the configuration for the shellinabox daemon.
# It is self-documenting: every variable reference includes a default value
# derived from the schema, and comments explain the purpose of each setting.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Daemon Start Control
# Controls whether the shellinaboxd service starts automatically.
# Value: 1 (yes) or 0 (no).
# Schema field: shellinabox_daemon_start
# Default: 1
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# shellinabox_daemon_start: {{ shellinabox_daemon_start | default(1) }}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web Server Port
# The TCP port on which shellinaboxd's embedded web server listens.
# Clients connect to this port via HTTP to access their terminal sessions.
# Schema field: shellinabox_port
# Default: 4200
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# shellinabox_port: {{ shellinabox_port | default(4200) }}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Daemon Arguments
# Optional arguments passed to the shellinaboxd daemon.
# These can include service definitions, custom CSS, security options, etc.
# Schema field: shellinabox_args
# Default: '--no-beep'
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# shellinabox_args: {{ shellinabox_args | default('--no-beep') }}

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Service Definitions (Generated from shellinabox_args if needed, or static defaults)
# Shellinabox uses a specific ini-style config for service definitions.
# However, the primary configuration for the daemon is often handled via
# the daemon arguments or a separate services config file.
# This template focuses on the main daemon parameters provided in the schema.
# If complex service definitions are needed, they are typically appended
# via shellinabox_args or handled by the role's logic.

# Example of how shellinabox might expect service definitions in a config file:
# [1:shell]
# command=/bin/bash
# no-auth=true
# css=/custom.css
#
# Note: The 'shellinabox_args' field usually overrides or supplements these.
# If you need specific service definitions, use the 'shellinabox_args' field
# to pass '--css-file' or define services via the 'shellinabox_services'
# variable if extended in the role's defaults.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# End of ShellInABox Configuration
